     "value": "Crystal structure analysis suggests that the protein should be classified within the N-terminal nucleophile (Ntn) hydrolase superfamily. Despite limited sequence similarity to known members, its overall fold and the organization of catalytic residues closely mirror those of several bacterial hydrolases (By similarity). PLBD1, a paralog, was recently identified as an aminopeptidase (By similarity)"
